Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.38,0:01:44.27,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,I owned a cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.76,0:01:46.83,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.89,0:01:50.60,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,A cop suddenly started speaking to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.05,0:01:53.25,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,Then there were two, then three of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.66,0:01:55.33,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,I thought, "If they take me in now,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.33,0:01:56.83,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,my cat is going to die."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.35,0:01:59.15,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,My place doesn't allow us to own them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.60,0:02:02.47,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,So I was the only one who knew about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.22,0:02:05.27,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}In Morioka City, Iwate Prefecture,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.27,0:02:07.23,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}in March of 2016,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.64,0:02:09.61,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}two people—\Na young girl and her mother—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.61,0:02:13.05,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}were found fatally stabbed \Nin their own home.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.52,0:02:15.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Morioka Prosecutor's Office
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.99,0:02:18.13,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}indicted Keita Oe, who lived nearby,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.13,0:02:21.29,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}on charges of felony murder and robbery.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.74,0:02:23.81,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}The events leading to \Nhis arrest were thus:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.33,0:02:28.54,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oe fled during police questioning \Nby officers on patrol,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.54,0:02:30.46,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}and after police chased \Nhim into his home,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.09,0:02:29.25,Default,Police,0,0,0,,Hey! Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.93,0:02:35.01,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}the officers who chased him discovered \Na blade with blood on it,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.40,0:02:37.97,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}and then arrested him \Nin flagrante delicto.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.76,0:02:41.04,Default,Police,0,0,0,,There he is!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.04,0:02:41.84,Default,Police,0,0,0,,Come on, behave!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.70,0:02:41.84,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Later DNA analysis
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.19,0:02:45.31,Default,Police,0,0,0,,Stop struggling!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.84,0:02:45.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}revealed the blood on the blade \Nmatched the victims' DNA.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.69,0:02:49.63,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oe consistently denied all \Nculpability for the crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.63,0:02:52.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}On the blade collected \Nas evidence, he insisted...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.08,0:02:53.42,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,I just picked it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.77,0:02:54.78,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,It wasn't mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.59,0:02:57.91,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,That's a bit hard to believe, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.91,0:03:01.83,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,I mean, he refused the questioning \Nbecause he felt guilty, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.34,0:03:05.51,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,No. He was previously a victim \Nof wrongful questioning
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.51,0:03:09.38,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,because an acquaintance of his \Nwas using drugs in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.38,0:03:11.89,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,You're saying that traumatized him?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.89,0:03:14.26,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,Even so, "I picked it up"?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.26,0:03:17.44,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,A bloody kitchen knife? Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.89,0:03:21.10,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,He claims he was planning to \Nturn it in to the police later.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.10,0:03:22.32,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,"Later"?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.33,0:03:24.71,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.71,0:03:26.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,His claims are all hard to believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.96,0:03:29.32,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,But when you consider Oe's background—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.32,0:03:33.30,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,the fact that he works as a live-in \Nemployee at a non-profit organization—
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.30,0:03:35.53,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,it starts sounding plausible.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.94,0:03:37.78,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,A non-profit?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.74,0:03:40.90,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,They work with the elderly \Nwho have no place to go,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.90,0:03:44.43,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,primarily running a shelter and providing \Nsupport for their independent living.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.43,0:03:47.91,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Oe's job was taking care \Nof the elderly there.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.33,0:03:51.16,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,However, they didn't pay him a wage.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.63,0:03:54.59,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,They only supplied him with goods \Nlike groceries, boxed lunches,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.59,0:03:57.35,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,and the occasional New Year's \Ngift of pocket money.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.68,0:03:59.41,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Yet despite that,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.41,0:04:02.85,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,they collected 50,000 yen \Na month from him as rent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.85,0:04:03.95,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,Brutal.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.37,0:04:07.94,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Apparently, quite a few of the \Nresidents have prior records.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.94,0:04:11.64,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Furthermore, the reason he was delayed in \Nturning over the weapon he found was...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.96,0:04:15.65,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,The rules say we can't call \Nany cop cars or ambulances.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.95,0:04:18.01,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,Because they'd bother the neighbors.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:19.90,0:04:23.06,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,That organization sounds \Nkinda shady, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 1,0:04:23.06,0:04:23.96,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:23.96,0:04:26.37,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It's extremely close to \Nbeing outright illegal.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:26.85,0:04:30.74,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,We've already seen an increase \Nin suspiciously managed NPOs
Dialogue: 1,0:04:30.74,0:04:33.92,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,since the earthquake relief funds \Nstarted flowing into this region.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.42,0:04:37.27,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,So it's not surprising the murder \Nweapon was just lying around.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.98,0:04:41.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,There's a good possibility Oe's innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.06,0:04:46.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,First, we'll investigate the \Norganization's activities and tax filings,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.47,0:04:49.35,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,then run background checks \Non all the residents.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.35,0:04:52.28,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'll focus on getting \Ninformation out of Oe.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.28,0:04:54.07,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You handle the investigation, Shimizu.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.07,0:04:57.57,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,You're dumping a huge job like \Nthat on me out of the blue?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.42,0:05:01.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Could you take care of his cat, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.08,0:05:02.16,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,The cat?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.11,0:05:06.78,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,{\i1}The commission for public defense cases \Nis low, despite how much work they take.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.11,0:05:09.36,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,{\i1}The public assumes he's guilty, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.36,0:05:12.12,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,{\i1}Plus, there's no suspended \Nsentence in murder cases,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.12,0:05:13.80,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,{\i1}and he could receive the death penalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.80,0:05:15.75,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's nothing to gain here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.91,0:05:21.97,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,Jeez, Higuruma{**-san}! Why did you \Ngo and accept a case like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.97,0:05:23.43,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It's fine every now and then.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.89,0:05:26.54,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,If we stuck to easy work, \Nour skills would dull.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.81,0:05:28.70,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's more than every now and then!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.02,0:05:30.86,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,It's more than every now and then!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.37,0:05:33.77,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You're saying your thoughts out loud.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.98,0:05:38.97,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,Sounds like Higuruma{**-kun} \Nhasn't changed then.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.54,0:05:42.86,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,It's rough when an independent \Nlawyer isn't in it for the money.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.32,0:05:48.62,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,At least it's not so bad that I'm being \Ntold to run a café on the side like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.62,0:05:50.50,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,But when you say he hasn't changed,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.50,0:05:52.91,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,you mean Higuruma{**-san}'s \Nalways been like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.91,0:05:54.66,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,Hm? No.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.13,0:05:57.77,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,I think he actually used to be worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.77,0:05:58.67,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.36,0:06:01.39,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,Back when he was with us,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.39,0:06:04.51,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,he was in charge of a case of \Nreckless driving resulting in injury.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.51,0:06:06.36,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,Oh, a drunk driving one.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.26,0:06:09.62,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,The defendant was nineteen,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.62,0:06:14.32,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,and his coworkers had coerced him into \Nboth the drinking and the driving.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.32,0:06:17.22,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,However, those involved all \Naligned their stories,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.22,0:06:19.15,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,and he wasn't able to prepare \Nmoney for a settlement,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.15,0:06:21.64,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,nor were we able to get \Nhim a suspended sentence.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.34,0:06:28.64,Default,Client,0,0,0,,Liar!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.37,0:06:33.12,Default,Client,0,0,0,,You said they'd find me innocent!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.83,0:06:37.84,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,You told him you'd manage to get \Na suspended sentence, though,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.84,0:06:40.32,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,not an innocent verdict.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.99,0:06:42.74,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,Have you learned your lesson now?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.74,0:06:45.98,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,Quit being a criminal defense \Nlawyer for impossible cases.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.56,0:06:50.60,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,Trying to save the weak \Nmay be a noble endeavor,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.99,0:06:53.55,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,but there's a limit to what \Nlawyers like us can do
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.55,0:06:56.08,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,without understanding from \Nthe courts and prosecutors.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.26,0:06:57.29,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Oh, I want to ride that!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.53,0:07:00.02,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,It's not worth continuing when \Nyour clients resent you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.78,0:07:05.98,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,They're at the end of their rope, \Nboth mentally and financially.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.39,0:07:08.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I can't blame them for lashing out at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.02,0:07:14.49,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,But what about your mental \Nstate, Higuruma{**-kun}?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.58,0:07:16.61,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.75,0:07:41.50,Default,Judge,0,0,0,,We find the defendant...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.94,0:07:43.20,Default,Judge,0,0,0,,innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.61,0:07:50.52,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,We actually won this case?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.41,0:07:53.65,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.17,0:07:57.02,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,They'll appeal right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.64,0:08:04.17,Default,Announcer,0,0,0,,{\i1}The prosecution has...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.30,0:08:17.80,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,Nothing stolen was found \Nin Oe{**-san}'s room.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.80,0:08:22.77,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,There was another person in the same NPO \Nwho went missing right after the crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.10,0:08:26.57,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,The fact that you were caught on a \Nconvenience store's security camera feed
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.57,0:08:30.92,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,during the time of the crime determined \Nfrom the corpse played a major role, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.35,0:08:34.41,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,Good thing you don't cook \Nfor yourself, Oe{**-san}!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.91,0:08:36.31,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,Counselor Higuruma...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.70,0:08:38.46,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.99,0:08:41.43,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,No need for "Counselor."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.43,0:08:44.57,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Besides, we're not in the clear yet. \NWe still have the second trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.79,0:08:47.21,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,That's not what I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.00,0:08:53.17,Default,Oe,0,0,0,,Thank you for believing me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.37,0:09:07.20,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}While defense lawyers have to work \Nwith limited budgets and manpower,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.20,0:09:11.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}prosecutors can pour manpower and \Ntaxpayer money into digging up evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.31,0:09:13.68,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's fine. That's how the system works.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.02,0:09:15.07,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}However,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.33,0:09:19.27,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}the prosecutors didn't submit any new \Nevidence during the second trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.27,0:09:24.96,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}The judge recognized \Ntheir absurd claim that
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.96,0:09:27.51,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}"there's no reason to suspect the \Nmissing person of the crime,"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.51,0:09:29.46,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}and they overturned the verdict.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.37,0:09:34.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}The highest court is always the \Nbottleneck for a third trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.47,0:09:37.06,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Most final appeals are \Nturned away at the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.06,0:09:39.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's challenging to even \Nget a proper trial there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.85,0:09:44.37,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}This trial was destined for a\Nguilty verdict from the start.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.67,0:09:53.03,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why are you
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.10,0:09:56.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}looking at me that way?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.48,0:10:03.62,Default,Takagi,0,0,0,,But what about your mental \Nstate, Higuruma{**-kun}?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.50,0:10:08.98,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'm not trying to tout the \Nideal of saving the weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.80,0:10:12.14,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It's just always gone against my nature
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.14,0:10:14.43,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,to leave things alone when \NI feel like they're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.04,0:10:17.58,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I've just never managed \Nto fix that habit.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.36,0:10:22.75,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The goddess of justice blinds her sight \Nto maintain fairness under the law,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.75,0:10:26.56,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,and people turn a blind eye to all \Nkinds of things to protect themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.97,0:10:31.26,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,But I don't want to brush away the \Nhands clinging to me for help,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.12,0:10:37.73,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,so I want to keep my eyes open, at least.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.06,0:10:44.76,Default,Judge,0,0,0,,If there are any objections \Nto today's trial,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.76,0:10:49.63,Default,Judge,0,0,0,,submit your final appeal in writing \Nwithin fifteen days, including today.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.18,0:11:02.89,Default,Shimizu,0,0,0,,Higuruma{**-san}?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.24,0:11:08.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Everyone come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.26,0:11:15.09,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,We're having a retrial.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.28,0:11:20.54,Default,Both,0,0,0,,Higuruma is in...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.62,0:11:22.41,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,...Ikebukuro.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.54,0:11:21.62,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,...Shinjuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.41,0:11:23.03,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Got it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.36,0:11:24.49,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Shinjuku?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.89,0:11:27.09,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I hope Itadori is heading there, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.09,0:11:28.61,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Ikebukuro, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.61,0:11:30.33,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder if Fushiguro's there, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.37,0:11:36.91,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Isn't she a little late?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.91,0:11:39.34,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,When is that girl
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.34,0:11:43.26,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,going to bring me my next sucker?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.55,0:11:53.15,Default,MaleStudent,0,0,0,,Huh? Wh-What?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.15,0:11:55.24,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Oh, no, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.24,0:11:56.86,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Not like that at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.86,0:11:59.47,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Hey, what are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.87,0:12:01.37,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Like this! This!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.37,0:12:03.12,Default,MaleStudent,0,0,0,,R-Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.12,0:12:04.86,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why are you keeping quiet?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.13,0:12:07.62,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're better off laughing!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.61,0:12:10.46,Default,Student,0,0,0,,Come on, come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.15,0:12:13.35,Default,MaleStudent,0,0,0,,What's your problem?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.35,0:12:13.99,Default,MaleStudent,0,0,0,,What's your problem?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.47,0:12:15.63,Default,Student,0,0,0,,There you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.89,0:12:18.28,Default,MaleStudent,0,0,0,,What's your problem?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.54,0:12:19.98,Default,MaleStudent,0,0,0,,What's your problem?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.06,0:12:13.43,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, dear. What did I tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.00,0:12:15.71,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not that I actually told you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.25,0:12:18.07,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}But why can't you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.07,0:12:19.55,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Are you an idiot?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.55,0:12:22.75,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}These guys aren't that smart or athletic,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.75,0:12:25.34,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}but they're brimming with pride.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.34,0:12:29.85,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}You just have to match their vibe and \Njoke around so you don't hurt that pride.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.49,0:12:34.10,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Then you won't get targeted \Nby anyone else, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.10,0:12:36.55,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you can occasionally \Nenjoy a good time, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.48,0:12:38.76,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Stop it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.02,0:12:43.98,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Here comes another idiot.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.98,0:12:46.32,Default,Student,0,0,0,,Is that uniform from West Middle?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.32,0:12:48.07,Default,Student,0,0,0,,You're a middle schooler?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.07,0:12:50.58,Default,Student,0,0,0,,You weren't showing respect, were you?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.58,0:12:53.45,Default,Student,0,0,0,,So you need to
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.45,0:12:54.66,Default,Student,0,0,0,,learn a lesson!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.40,0:12:56.25,Default,Student,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.70,0:13:02.70,Default,Student,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.29,0:13:12.55,Default,Student,0,0,0,,No violence!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.97,0:13:18.52,Default,Student,0,0,0,,Come here!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.25,0:13:30.30,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What about you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.74,0:13:35.74,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,M-Me?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.81,0:13:37.75,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.75,0:13:39.10,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.10,0:13:42.32,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,You aren't planning to go through \NIkebukuro to reach Shinjuku, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.88,0:13:44.74,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,That area's rich with supplies.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.23,0:13:47.64,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,We're more likely to \Nencounter other Players.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.90,0:13:50.63,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,There are two reasons for going this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.63,0:13:52.55,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,The route is easy to follow,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.55,0:13:54.79,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,and I have a base nearby.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.34,0:13:58.69,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,At least let me take a shower.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.69,0:14:01.34,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,I haven't gotten much \Nrest since yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.34,0:14:07.40,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Higuruma uses this theater as his base.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.40,0:14:09.45,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Assuming he hasn't moved, that is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.45,0:14:10.71,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Cool!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.71,0:14:13.02,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You've been a big help! Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.55,0:14:16.13,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Oh, h-h-hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.45,0:14:17.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.85,0:14:19.65,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,Are you seriously going?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.65,0:14:23.46,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I'd rather reunite with my friend \Nfirst, but we're in a hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.79,0:14:26.51,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,I haven't met Higuruma myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.51,0:14:29.97,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,but he once beat Haba{**-san} to a pulp.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.97,0:14:31.59,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Then I'll be fine!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.59,0:14:35.27,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I beat that propeller head, too, \Nso I'll at least be able to run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.84,0:14:37.96,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,See you later!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.73,0:14:40.95,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Say it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.22,0:14:43.76,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Say it, man!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.68,0:14:46.76,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}You should stop doing this!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.52,0:14:53.69,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm sorry,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.88,0:14:56.12,Default,Amai,0,0,0,,{\i1}Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.97,0:15:02.46,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Higuruma? Oh...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.46,0:15:06.13,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Sorry, but I'm Reggie.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.13,0:15:09.19,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,She deceived you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.71,0:15:14.48,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Don't give me that look.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.48,0:15:16.78,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,I'm not frightened at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.78,0:15:18.43,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,Just so you know, Reggie—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.43,0:15:19.23,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Stop talking.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.18,0:15:24.37,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Oho?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.96,0:15:27.82,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,We're wasting time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.71,0:15:39.74,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Who's there?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.19,0:15:42.24,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,What are you doing over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.13,0:15:45.36,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I could ask you that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.12,0:15:51.90,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Have you ever taken a bath \Nwhile in your clothes?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.90,0:15:53.01,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Never.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.82,0:15:56.94,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It feels better than I expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.52,0:16:00.63,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.55,0:16:04.54,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Back when I was in elementary school,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.54,0:16:07.58,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I loved our classes on \Nswimming in clothes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.23,0:16:11.83,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,So many things have stopped \Nmattering lately,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.83,0:16:16.44,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,so I've been challenging myself to \Ntry things I assumed I shouldn't do.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.44,0:16:19.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I've basically gone off the \Nrails after hitting my mid-30s.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.99,0:16:21.04,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Is that funny?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.59,0:16:23.53,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,It's kind of amusing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.05,0:16:25.87,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You're Higuruma, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.35,0:16:27.82,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,In the flesh.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.82,0:16:28.96,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I want to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.78,0:16:31.93,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Hold on. Wait, wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.26,0:16:34.06,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'm a lawyer.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.06,0:16:38.67,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Talking to me will incur a consultation \Nfee of 5,000 yen every half hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.67,0:16:39.52,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.36,0:16:42.81,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'm kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.81,0:16:45.82,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I just wanted to try acting \Nlike a nasty lawyer for once.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.86,0:16:48.35,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.89,0:16:50.93,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}What's this guy doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.55,0:16:53.52,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You have 100 points, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.19,0:16:56.62,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's not a past sorcerer \Nwho's been incarnated.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.87,0:16:59.90,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's a modern sorcerer whose \Ntechnique was activated!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.90,0:17:01.41,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}We can talk it out!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.41,0:17:02.94,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's room for negotiation!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.36,0:17:05.61,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah. You pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.96,0:17:06.75,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.75,0:17:09.01,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That's enough. I can tell now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.01,0:17:10.96,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That's quite the shikigami.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.96,0:17:12.52,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,You're strong, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.52,0:17:16.31,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,If you were weak, I'd just \Nkill you as another mark.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.31,0:17:17.52,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,But you're good.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.52,0:17:18.89,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Let's work together.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.89,0:17:20.24,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}What gives?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.24,0:17:21.83,Default,Remi,0,0,0,,{\i1}I never heard about this!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.96,0:17:24.81,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What are you getting at?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.81,0:17:28.47,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,How much do you know \Nabout this Culling Game?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.17,0:17:30.45,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,It's a ritual, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.97,0:17:34.22,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,It uses the cursed energy of \Nthe Players inside the barriers
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.22,0:17:36.79,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,to ferry the people of \NJapan to the other side
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.79,0:17:39.08,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,and change them into something inhuman.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.71,0:17:42.17,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}Guess I should stay quiet \Nabout {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama}.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.17,0:17:45.81,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Oh? Do you know Kenjaku, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.87,0:17:48.67,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew there'd be one!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.13,0:17:51.65,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}A sorcerer connected to Kenjaku!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.48,0:17:54.78,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Uh, so, to be frank,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.59,0:17:59.00,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,we want to stop the Culling Game.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.77,0:18:01.05,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Er, time out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.05,0:18:04.55,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,When I say "stop it," I mean we want \Nto negate the compulsory killing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.95,0:18:08.79,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Please let us use your 100 points \Nto add a rule toward that end.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.31,0:18:11.44,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Allow me to be frank, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.01,0:18:13.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I refuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.76,0:18:16.29,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Is that another joke?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.10,0:18:18.17,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.17,0:18:21.70,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I just sense potential \Nin the Culling Game.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.13,0:18:24.16,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Sometimes the law is powerless.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.16,0:18:27.62,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,But what about the rules \Nof this Culling Game?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.62,0:18:30.21,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,If the power I've been granted is real,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.21,0:18:32.09,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,then those rules must be, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.09,0:18:36.46,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,What you just said about Players' \Ncursed energy being used?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.46,0:18:38.29,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,That's probably a bluff.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.29,0:18:39.10,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.10,0:18:44.28,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Well, less of a bluff, \Nand more Plan B or C.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.28,0:18:46.06,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,I have three reasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.56,0:18:48.25,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The number of Players.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.25,0:18:50.15,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The strength gap between Players.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.15,0:18:51.85,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The barriers' rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.29,0:18:57.32,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,If roughly 1,000 people were equally \Nsplit up between the ten Colonies,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.32,0:18:59.85,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,that would be 100 per Colony.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.85,0:19:03.13,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,But among the Players are sorcerers
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.13,0:19:05.16,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,like Kashimo or Higuruma,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.16,0:19:06.81,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,who are much stronger than the rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.81,0:19:10.77,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,These two alone have already \Nculled sixty sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.77,0:19:14.37,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,There's probably one like \Nthem in each Colony.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.79,0:19:17.61,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,So the weak are weeded out early on,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.61,0:19:19.99,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,and the Culling Game \Nwill reach a stalemate?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.67,0:19:22.63,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}I certainly did sense that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.99,0:19:25.29,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Colony has been too quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.29,0:19:26.89,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,It already has.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.89,0:19:29.93,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,At least here in Tokyo No. 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.93,0:19:33.82,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,On top of that, there's the teleportation \Nwhen people enter the Colony.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.82,0:19:36.07,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,It serves to spread them out,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.07,0:19:38.14,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,but its main goal is likely to encourage
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.14,0:19:40.61,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,an early second awakening \Nof modern sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.61,0:19:43.33,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,There are some who die during \Nthe teleportation, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.33,0:19:46.24,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,If he was really trying to use \Nthe Players' cursed energy,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.24,0:19:48.87,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,he would want the greatest \Nnumber of sorcerers
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.87,0:19:51.58,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,to fight for the longest time possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.58,0:19:56.33,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,What if people who broke the \Nrules were punished by physics,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.33,0:20:00.33,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,without any need for indictments, \Nprosecutions, or arguments at trials?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.33,0:20:02.65,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Wouldn't that be wonderful?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.65,0:20:04.94,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'll acknowledge there are \Nissues with the current rules,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.94,0:20:08.30,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,but I want to watch over the system \Nserving as a basis for this game.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.30,0:20:10.80,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It won't do for it to end too soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.80,0:20:13.75,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'd especially love to witness \Nthe stripping of a technique
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.75,0:20:16.56,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,mentioned in Rule 2 and 8 at least once.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.94,0:20:19.87,Default,Shoko,0,0,0,,It's better for the rules if \Nbeing stripped means death, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.32,0:20:23.22,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,The Culling Game itself is a ritual.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.22,0:20:26.30,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,If we take too long, \Nevery person in this nation will die.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.30,0:20:27.65,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,That's a lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.65,0:20:30.74,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The Culling Game insists \Non its own permanence.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.74,0:20:33.11,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't really get that part, either!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.50,0:20:37.18,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Let me rephrase it, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.91,0:20:41.30,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Let me use your 100 points, Higuruma!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.72,0:20:46.67,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Have you ever killed someone \Nwho ticked you off?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.81,0:20:54.16,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It feels much better than I expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.00,0:20:56.21,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}A shikigami?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.36,0:20:59.21,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Higuruma has 100 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.21,0:21:01.64,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}He might have killed \Ntwenty sorcerers already.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.19,0:21:03.87,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't leap in recklessly.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.33,0:21:05.69,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll go on defense,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.69,0:21:08.18,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I'll be ready to \Nrespond to any attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.17,0:21:11.78,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Domain Expansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.65,0:21:14.73,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Deadly Sentencing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.90,0:21:32.43,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,The rules' idea of continuation is \Njust a cover for the real plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.43,0:21:34.41,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Mark my words.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.41,0:21:36.87,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,When only the strong remain,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.87,0:21:39.52,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,Kenjaku is going to drop \Na bomb on the game,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.52,0:21:43.27,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,and the Culling Game \Nwill fulfill its purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.73,0:23:42.45,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Now, make your argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.45,0:23:43.53,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What happens if I'm judged guilty?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.53,0:23:44.96,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Judgeman, please begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.96,0:23:45.89,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You mean I can lie?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.89,0:23:47.61,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You get one chance to make a statement.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.61,0:23:48.84,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I can't control cursed energy!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.84,0:23:51.78,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,How can he hold his own against \Nme without cursed energy?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.78,0:23:53.90,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I want a retrial! One more time!
